     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "One: program order. A core that writes X, and later reads X, gets back its own value, as long as no one else wrote in between."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "def[0]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Two: writes become visible. A write by one core is eventually seen by reads on the others, if the reads come long enough afterwards. Our example broke this rule."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "def[1]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Three: write serialization. Two writes to the same location are seen by every core in the same order. Nobody may see 1 then 2, while someone else sees 2 then 1."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "def[2]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Coherence is about one location. Consistency, a different question, is about when writes to different locations become visible relative to each other. That comes in a later video."
